; Regression for PR.md 1.1: lambda_release_zero decremented cons tails with a
; plain read-modify-write, so two pmap workers freeing lists that share a tail
; lost reference-count updates and corrupted memory.
;
; Every pmap result element is (sum (cons i t)): the new cons shares the same
; tail t, and freeing the result concurrently decrements t->rc from several
; workers.  The outer loop repeats the race internally so one process run is
; enough to catch it (reproducing it used to need dozens of process runs).
mk → (λn.
  t → (range 0 50)
  f → (λi. (sum (cons i t)))
  spin → (λk acc.
    if (== k 0)
    then acc
    else (spin (- k 1) (+ acc (sum (pmap f (range 0 4000))))))
  (spin n 0))
(mk 40)
